---
description: NumPy-style docstrings for public functions
globs: src/skimage/**/*.py,src/_skimage2/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

- Public functions use NumPy-style docstrings.
- Describe parameters and return values.
- Document an image array parameter as `image : ndarray of shape (M, N)`.
- Refer to `M` and `N` for those dimensions when the description needs them.

```python
def normalize(image):
    """Scale image intensities to the unit interval.

    Parameters
    ----------
    image : ndarray of shape (M, N)
        Input image with M rows and N columns.

    Returns
    -------
    out : ndarray of shape (M, N)
        Normalized image with the same M rows and N columns.
    """
```
